From: Jules AI <jules@google.com>
Date: Sat, 6 Dec 2025 20:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Fix Cross-Region Block Explosions

This patch fixes a thread-safety issue where explosions
could attempt to destroy blocks in a different, unloaded,
or otherwise inaccessible region, causing a server crash.

The logic for destroying a block is extracted into a new
private method, `explodeBlock`.

The main loop in `finalizeExplosion` is modified to check
if a block's position is owned by the current region. If not,
it schedules the `explodeBlock` call to the appropriate
region's scheduler, ensuring thread-safe block destruction
across region boundaries.

